[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606012100-donation-funded-operation-and-compute-node-participation", :adr/title "ADR-2606012100: Donation-Funded Operation (明記 on etzhayyim.com) + Compute/Node-Participation as In-Kind Donation (ameno browser inference / e7m CLI node / kotoba pod)", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606012100: Donation-Funded Operation + Compute/Node-Participation as In-Kind Donation\n\n**Date**: 2026-06-01\n**Status**: PROPOSED\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ ≥3 (ratify), 30-day public objection period\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Implements the public-facing side of ADR-2605192115 §6 (公開証跡) and extends ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only fleet) with a *donated-node* fleet class. Sibling to ADR-2605301036 (cash mission-funding) — this ADR adds the **in-kind compute** funding modality. Does **not** amend any constitutional invariant.\n\n## Context\n\nTwo gaps, one ADR.\n\n**(1) etzhayyim.com does not say it runs on donations.** ADR-2605192115 locks `non_profit_only` + `donation_only` and §6 requires a public, third-party-auditable proof of non-profit operation. Today the apex (`https://etzhayyim.com/`) reverse-proxies to the yoro app (`50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/src/worker.ts` §4) and nowhere states, in plain language a visitor can read, that the religious-corp is funded only by donation and that no money ever reaches an adherent as cash (Basic High Income N1, ADR-2605301020). The donation policy is real and constitutional but invisible to the public it should reassure.\n\n**(2) Donation is defined only as money.** The `purpose` enum (`com.etzhayyim.apps.payment.sent`) and the `give.*` lexicons treat a donation as a USDC transfer routed through `TitheRouter.donate()`. But the mission's two scarcest non-cash resources are **inference compute** (Murakumo-only per ADR-2605215000 — deliberately *not* rentable from commercial GPU clouds, so capacity is genuinely constrained) and **substrate durability** (kotoba blocks / IPFS pinning / Datom replication). A supporter with a phone, a laptop, or a spare machine can give *those* directly. There is no doctrine that recognizes **donating compute** as a donation — even though it is the most mission-aligned gift available and the one the Charter's GPU constraints make most valuable.\n\nThe directive: **明記 donation-funded operation on etzhayyim.com, and design donation to include node participation — ameno/Murakumo browser inference, the e7m CLI, and kotoba pods.**\n\nThe hard constraint is that several invariants are constitutional and are **not** amended here:\n- `non_profit_only` / `donation_only` / 広告排除 (ADR-2605192100 §2; ADR-2605192115; Charter Rider §2).\n- **Murakumo-only inference** — LiteLLM `127.0.0.1:4000` + EVO-X2 LAN + per-node Ollama `gemma3:4b`; **no RunPod / no commercial GPU rental** (ADR-2605215000; Charter Rider §2(i)).\n- **baien edge-target** — any browser inference must run inside the WASM-32 + iPhone 12+ + Android 4GB envelope on frozen edge models (ADR-2605241900).\n- **No server-side signing key** — the religious-corp holds no donor key (ADR-2605231525).\n- **Anti-class / N2 no-make-work / N3 no-coercion** — no gift may become a path to benefits (ADR-2605261000; ADR-2605301020 §7).\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. 明記: etzhayyim.com declares donation-funded operation\n\nThe apex Worker (`50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/`) serves **two new local routes** (before the §4 yoro proxy fallback), cookie-free and tracker-free by construction (Charter Rider §2(c)):\n\n| Route | Content | Audience |\n|---|---|---|\n| `GET /donate` | Human-readable HTML: \"etzhayyim is a 宗教法人 operated **only on donation**. We take no advertising, sell nothing, and never pay any member cash. You can give **money** or **compute**.\" + the three node-participation options. | Visitors |\n| `GET /.well-known/donation.json` | Machine-readable donation policy: entity DID, accepted purposes, cash rail (TitheRouter), the three in-kind compute-node modalities + their endpoints/gates. Analogue of `/.well-known/did.json`. | Agents / crawlers / wallets |\n\nBoth are static, no JS required to read the policy, no external resource, no cookie, `Permissions-Policy: interest-cohort=(), browsing-topics=()` (matching the existing DID-doc headers). The page is **information about etzhayyim's own religious activity**, which §1.2 of ADR-2605192115 explicitly classifies as *not advertising*.\n\n### 2. Two donation media (cash + compute), one purpose\n\nA donation is now any of:\n\n| Medium | Rail | purpose | Titheable? | Accounting |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Cash** (USDC) | `TitheRouter.donate()` on Base L2 | `donation` / `kisha` / `grant` | ✅ 90/10 split (ADR-2605192130) | on-chain tx |\n| **Compute / storage** (in-kind) | join the Murakumo mesh + kotoba substrate as a donated node | `donation` (in-kind sub-type `compute`) | **❌ non-titheable** (no USDC to split — §5) | imputed-value attestation (toritate, aggregate-only) |\n\nIn-kind compute donation is the **mirror image** of Basic High Income (ADR-2605301020): there, the religious-corp values in-kind *provision* to adherents at market-equivalent for transparency while no cash crosses; here, a donor's in-kind *contribution* is valued at market-equivalent for transparency while no cash crosses. **No `purpose` enum change is required** — compute donation is a `donation` whose medium is recorded in a `give.computeDonationAttestation`, not a new payment purpose.\n\n### 3. The three node-participation forms\n\nAll three join the **Murakumo mesh as donated first-party fleet nodes** (never commercial rental — §4) and/or the **kotoba substrate** (ADR-2605262130) as block/replication nodes.\n\n| Form | What the donor runs | Contributes | Constitutional envelope |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **(a) ameno browser inference** | Opens a consent-gated tab; ameno runs WebGPU/WebNN inference on **frozen baien edge models** in-browser (WASM-32). Zero install. | Inference capacity to the mesh while the tab is open and consent is active. | baien edge-target (ADR-2605241900): WASM-32 + iPhone 12+ + Android 4GB; frozen encoders; device power-budget (G8). |\n| **(b) e7m CLI node** | `e7m node join` registers a laptop/workstation as an Ollama (`gemma3:4b`) + WASM inference endpoint and/or a kotoba light node. | Inference + optional block storage; survives across sessions. | Murakumo-fleet membership (ADR-2605215000); donor-held key (ADR-2605231525). |\n| **(c) kotoba pod** | A kotoba pod (IPFS block backend + Datom replication, optional Ollama) joins the substrate. | Substrate durability (pinning, Datom replication) + optional inference. | kotoba substrate (ADR-2605262130 / 2605312345); Charter Rider §2(i) — donor's own hardware, not rented GPU. |\n\nThe mesh treats donated nodes exactly as core Murakumo nodes for **inference routing** (LiteLLM gateway view) but tags them `donated` so toritate can attest the in-kind contribution and so capacity planning never assumes a donated node is always present (G9 honesty: donated capacity is best-effort, not an SLA).\n\n### 4. Murakumo-only reconciliation (the load-bearing invariant)\n\nADR-2605215000 makes the Murakumo fleet the **sole** inference SSoT and forbids RunPod / commercial GPU rental. A donated node is consistent with — indeed *strengthens* — that invariant, because:\n\n1. **It IS a Murakumo node.** A donated browser/CLI/pod node joins the same LiteLLM-fronted mesh (`127.0.0.1:4000` from the caller's view; donated nodes are reachable mesh members). It is not a third-party cloud; it is fleet expansion by gift.\n2. **It is the donor's own hardware, uncompensated.** Charter Rider §2(i)'s prohibition is on *commercial GPU rental* — paying a cloud (or being paid) for compute. A gift of one's own device is the opposite of a rental: **no payment in either direction** (G2). Compute donation is never compensated; \"rent us your GPU for money\" is prohibited (it would be commercial + would make the donor a vendor).\n3. **It does not touch the vendor's commercial pool.** The vendor (`etzhayyim.com` commercial arm, ADR-2605301036) keeps its own GPU pool for paid SaaS; religious-corp callers still must not invoke it. Donated nodes are religious-corp mesh members, a separate population from the vendor pool.\n\nThis ADR therefore **extends the ADR-2605215000 fleet definition** with a `donated` node class (addendum, not amendment): `fleet = core nodes (EVO-X2 + Mac minis) ∪ donated nodes (ameno/e7m/kotoba)`. The no-commercial-GPU and Murakumo-only invariants stand unchanged.\n\n### 5. Tithe + accounting reconciliation\n\n- **Non-titheable.** The 10% TitheRouter split (ADR-2605192130) operates on a USDC amount; an in-kind compute donation moves no USDC, so there is nothing to split — the same structural reason `kisha` is exempt (ADR-2605192130 §5). **100% of donated compute serves the mission directly** (actor inference + baien training-adjacent edge work + substrate durability); none is skimmed because none is cash.\n- **Imputed-value attestation.** toritate (ADR-2605262900) values donated compute at a market-equivalent reference (inference-tokens served / GPU-equiv-hours / storage-GB·days), method-versioned and Council-attested, **aggregate-only, no donor PII** — exactly the imputed-value method of ADR-2605301020 §4, applied to inbound in-kind gifts. Published as a transparency figure, never as a per-donor leaderboard (anti-class, §6).\n- **N1 untouched.** Compute donation flows *into* the mission; it never becomes adherent cash. `cashStipendUsdMicros ≡ 0` (ADR-2605301020) is unaffected.\n\n### 6. Gates (constitutional invariants, enforced)\n\n| Gate | Rule | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G1 consent-only** | Browser node never auto-starts; explicit opt-in per session; CLI/pod join is an explicit command. Stop = close tab / `e7m node leave`. | Charter Rider §2(c); ADR-2605231525 consent-capability |\n| **G2 uncompensated gift** | No payment to the donor for compute, ever (that would be commercial GPU rental + make the donor a vendor). Donation only. | ADR-2605215000; Charter Rider §2(i) |\n| **G3 Murakumo-mesh-only** | Donated nodes join the Murakumo fleet / kotoba substrate; never a commercial cloud path; religious-corp inference stays Murakumo-only. | ADR-2605215000 |\n| **G4 no quid-pro-quo (anti-class)** | Compute donation is **never** a path to Liberation-stage advancement, benefits, or priority. Benefits remain capacity-gated + pooled; donating more compute buys nothing for the donor. | ADR-2605261000 N2/N3; ADR-2605301020 §7 |\n| **G5 non-titheable in-kind** | No USDC split on in-kind compute; 100% to mission; imputed-value accounted for transparency only. | ADR-2605192130 §5; ADR-2605301020 §4 |\n| **G6 no-server-key** | Donor holds their own node key (donor DID or ephemeral node DID); religious-corp holds no donor credential. | ADR-2605231525 |\n| **G7 cookie-free / no-tracking** | `/donate`, `/.well-known/donation.json`, and the browser node carry no cookie, no analytics, no third-party script. | Charter Rider §2(c); ADR-2605192115 §1.2 |\n| **G8 Wellbecoming device-budget** | Browser/CLI inference respects a power/thermal budget + user pause; honest about battery/heat impact; no dark-pattern \"keep contributing\" nag. | ADR-2605192100 §1.13 |\n| **G9 outward-gated + honesty** | Live mesh-enrollment of external donor nodes = Council + operator (R0 = design + page + lexicon + e7m/kotoba scaffolding). Donated capacity is best-effort, never an SLA, and labelled as such. | ADR-2605192100 §1.12 outward-action gating |\n\n### 7. Implementation surface\n\n- **Worker** (`50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/src/worker.ts`): add `GET /donate` (HTML) + `GET /.well-known/donation.json` (machine-readable) routes, served locally before the yoro proxy; cookie-free headers reused from the DID-doc branch.\n- **Lexicon** (`00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/give/`): new `computeDonationAttestation.json` — aggregate, period-scoped, no PII: `{ period, nodeClass: ameno|e7m|kotoba, imputedValueUsdMicros, inferenceTokensServed, storageGbDays, titheable: false (const) }`. Update `give/README.edn`.\n- **e7m CLI** (`70-tools/`): `e7m node join|leave|status` design stub — registers/withdraws a donated Murakumo/kotoba node; R0 documents the surface, live enrollment gated (G9).\n- **deps.toml**: `[[adrs]]` registry entry + a `[donation]` section (media, node classes, gates) as machine-readable SSoT.\n- **No Solidity change** — cash rail is the existing TitheRouter; compute donation has no on-chain settlement (it is in-kind).\n- **No `purpose` enum change** — compute donation is a `donation` recorded via the new attestation lexicon.\n\n## Consequences\n\n**Positive**:\n- etzhayyim.com now plainly states donation-funded, ad-free, no-adherent-cash operation — satisfying the ADR-2605192115 §6 public-proof intent in human- and machine-readable form.\n- The Charter's hardest constraint (Murakumo-only, no commercial GPU) becomes a **participation invitation**: supporters expand the exact capacity the Charter refuses to rent, by gift. Scarcity → community contribution.\n- A new, highly mission-aligned funding modality with **zero** invariant amendments: compute donation rides the existing fleet + substrate, accounted like imputed income in reverse.\n- Browser node = zero-install onboarding for non-technical supporters; e7m/kotoba = deeper commitment paths.\n\n**Negative / risks**:\n- **Sybil / poisoned-inference risk** from anonymous donated nodes. Mitigation: donated nodes serve only frozen edge models (no training from donor nodes); inference results that feed governance/actor decisions are cross-checked against core nodes; donated capacity is advisory/best-effort (G9), and high-trust paths can pin to core nodes.\n- **\"Donate compute → get benefits\" misread** (quid-pro-quo / prosperity-gospel optics). Mitigation: G4 hard rule + the /donate page states explicitly that giving compute earns the donor nothing and is a pure gift.\n- **Device harm / battery drain** if browser inference is greedy. Mitigation: G8 power-budget + user pause + honest disclosure; default conservative.\n- **Capacity-planning hazard** if donated nodes are assumed present. Mitigation: `donated` tag + best-effort SLA (G9); core fleet sizing never depends on donated capacity.\n- **Valuation contestability** of imputed compute-value (same class of risk as ADR-2605301020). Mitigation: method-versioned, Council-attested, open valuation table; figures explicitly imputed.\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n1. **Cash donations only; no compute modality.** Rejected: ignores the most mission-aligned gift the Charter's GPU constraints make uniquely valuable, and leaves Murakumo capacity bottlenecked with no community-expansion path.\n2. **Pay donors for compute (compute marketplace).** Rejected: that is commercial GPU rental (Charter Rider §2(i)) and turns the donor into a vendor — directly violates Murakumo-only + non-profit. Donation must be uncompensated (G2).\n3. **Route donated browser/cloud compute through a commercial GPU aggregator.** Rejected: violates ADR-2605215000 (no RunPod / commercial GPU). Donated nodes must join the Murakumo mesh as first-party members.\n4. **Add a `compute-donation` payment purpose enum.** Rejected: in-kind compute has no USDC settlement; overloading the on-chain payment enum misrepresents it. A `give.computeDonationAttestation` (imputed-value, off-chain, aggregate) is the honest record.\n5. **Make compute donation titheable (notional 10%).** Rejected: nothing to split (no cash); mirrors the kisha exemption (ADR-2605192130 §5). 100% serves the mission directly.\n6. **Condition Liberation-stage priority on compute donated** (contribution → reward). Rejected: violates anti-class N6 + N2/N3 (ADR-2605261000) and the abundance-without-accumulation principle (ADR-2605301020 §7). G4 forbids it.\n7. **Put the donation notice in the yoro app instead of the apex Worker.** Rejected: the apex Worker is the self-contained, cookie-free, always-on surface (same place as the DID doc); the §6 public proof should not depend on the SPA's runtime.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605192100 (Mission Charter — non_profit_only / donation_only; §1.12 outward gating; §1.13 Wellbecoming)\n- ADR-2605192115 (Non-profit / donation-only / no-ads — §1.2 \"案内 is not advertising\"; §6 public proof)\n- ADR-2605192130 (TitheRouter 10% auto-split — cash rail; §5 kisha non-titheable precedent)\n- ADR-2605192145 (Public Fund — destination of cash donations)\n- ADR-2605215000 (Murakumo-only inference — the fleet donated nodes join; no RunPod / commercial GPU)\n- ADR-2605241900 (baien edge-target invariant — ameno browser inference envelope)\n- ADR-2605301020 (Basic High Income — imputed-value method, reused here for inbound in-kind; N1 cash≡0; §7 anti-class)\n- ADR-2605301036 (Mission-Funding Earned-Revenue Arm — cash funding sibling; vendor GPU pool boundary)\n- ADR-2605262130 / 2605312345 (kotoba storage substrate — kotoba pod nodes)\n- ADR-2605262900 (toritate — imputed-value attestation of donated compute)\n- ADR-2605231525 (No server-side signing key — donor holds keys)\n- `50-infra/etzhayyim-did-web/src/worker.ts` (apex Worker — /donate + /.well-known/donation.json)\n- `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/give/` (donation-side lexicons)\n</content>\n</invoke>\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606012100-donation-funded-operation-and-compute-node-participation.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "donation-funded-operation-and-compute-node-participation", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-01", :adr/date "2026-06-01", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605192100-etzhayyim-mission-charter" "adr-2605192115-etzhayyim-non-profit-donation-only-no-ads" "adr-2605192130-etzhayyim-tithe-redistribution" "adr-2605192145-etzhayyim-public-fund-architecture" "adr-2605215000-etzhayyim-inference-murakumo-only-no-runpod" "adr-2605241900-baien-edge-target-invariant" "adr-2605301020-basic-high-income-imputed-and-commons-asset-doctrine" "adr-2605301036-mission-funding-earned-revenue-arm" "adr-2605262130-kotoba-storage-substrate-unification" "adr-2605262900-toritate-accounting-audit" "adr-2605231525-etzhayyim-no-server-side-signing-key"], :adr/authoritative_for ["public declaration on etzhayyim.com that the religious-corp operates on donation only (the /donate page + /.well-known/donation.json)" "the in-kind COMPUTE donation modality (donating compute/storage to the Murakumo mesh + kotoba substrate counts as donation)" "the three node-participation forms — ameno browser inference, e7m CLI node, kotoba pod — and their constitutional gates" "how in-kind compute donation reconciles with Murakumo-only inference, no-commercial-GPU, tithe, and anti-class invariants"]}]
